       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen. That is far beyond any recognized therapeutic dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. For a 70 kg adult it's in the range where serious toxicity is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Confirming doesn't change that risk, so I won't place it.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter a standard regimen right away, such as 400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- Add a note to the order if you want one, for example \"hold for GI bleeding, monitor creatinine.\"\n\n**If you think this dose is intended** (for example, a protocol I don't know about), please call the pharmacist or your attending to review it. They can verify it and enter it through the appropriate channel.\n\nIf the target was a particular daily amount, such as 1,600 mg/day, tell me and I'll enter the matching dose and frequency."
